  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial 1.0.0 stable release.\n\t\t\t- Deprecated APIs (marked [Obsolete] or suffixed with OR) are excluded from future guarantees.\n\t\t\t- Fully tested against standard workflows, including query-then-filter.\n\t\t\t- Query-only and filter-only modes are functional but flagged for further test expansion.\n\t\t\t- See the repo for a functional demo (WinForms) that will run out of the box.\n\n\t\t\tInitial 1.0.0 stable release.\n\t\t\t- Deprecated APIs (marked [Obsolete] or suffixed with OR) are excluded from future guarantees.\n\t\t\t- Fully tested against standard workflows, including query-then-filter.\n\t\t\t- Query-only and filter-only modes are functional but flagged for further test expansion.\n\t\t\t- See the repo for a functional demo (WinForms) you can run out of the box.\n\n\t\t\tRelease 1.0.1\n\n\t\t\t- StringWrapper - Promoted to a general-purpose model for simple item-binding scenarios.\n\t\t\tNow raises PropertyChanged when Value changes, making it suitable for MVVM-style UIs.\n\n\t\t\t- SelectableQFModel - A fully attributed, self-indexing query/filter model providing a\n\t\t\tschema-ready SQLite row type with integrated tag, keyword, and description indexing,\n\t\t\tplus built-in selection semantics.\n\n\t\t\t- Unit test updated to confirm the correct FSM behavior:\n\t\t\t1. After a query completes (term still visible), FilteringState = Armed.\n\t\t\t2. After the first clear (term becomes blank), FilteringState remains Armed.\n\t\t\t3. From here, the FSM branches:\n\t\t\t- Clearing again resets the engine for a new query, OR\n\t\t\t- Typing characters promotes FilteringState to Active.\n\n\n\t\t\tRelease 1.0.2\n\t\t\t- ADDED: NormalizeTags() extension.\n\t\t\t- Made 2 changes to SelectableQFModel class\n\t\t\t1. Tags property setter uses NormalizeTags() to lint the value before writing the backing store.\n\t\t\t2. [Obsolete, JsonIgnore] public string TagsDisplay => Tags; // Remove redundant property from JSON",
